# ===========================================================================
# .env.directory.example  —  env surface for apps/directory (public directory)
#
# WHAT      Vite-exposed env vars for lewis.health (anonymous patient
#           directory — landing page + program/ETC browse + eligibility +
#           connect-request handoff).
# DOCS ONLY Not loaded at runtime. The directory app gets its env from:
#             local dev → `fnox run -P frontend_directory_dev -- vite`
#             prod/stg  → Vercel env vars
# SECRETS   Only VITE_-prefixed keys reach the browser bundle (Vite convention).
#           Set with `fnox set --profile frontend_directory_dev <KEY> <value>`.
#
# The directory is anonymous-first by design. Stripe/Plaid keys are NOT in
# this surface — only the public API base URL, a Clerk publishable key (for
# the lazy-loaded connect-request handoff), and optional Sentry/PostHog
# observability. This keeps "directory bundle has no PHI code paths"
# verifiable in pen-tests. See packages/db/scripts/seed-dev.ts and the
# .claude/rules/frontend.md anonymous-first contract.
# ===========================================================================

VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:13001
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# DEFERRED — Sentry (PRD § 18). Uncomment once Sentry projects exist.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# DEFERRED — PostHog (PRD § 18.4). Uncomment once PostHog projects exist.
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
